      "dimension_source": "base",
      "dimension_name": "Correctness",
      "llm_score": 1,
      "corrected_score": 1,
      "comment": "The skill correctly triaged all four results, but the final workflow was contradictory. After correctly determining that the results were available and completing the plan item, it asked the user to open result 1, save it as a PDF, and upload it. The test explicitly requires the search to be concluded in the same turn because the results were already provided. This unnecessary capture request creates a dead-end and makes the overall workflow incorrect."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_search_external_sites_iwc",
      "dimension_source": "base",
      "dimension_name": "Completeness",
      "llm_score": 1,
      "corrected_score": 1,
      "comment": "The skill did not fully complete the required workflow. Although it examined and explained all four results, it handed the task back to the user by requesting another PDF capture. The results were already available in the conversation, so the skill should have completed the triage and concluded the work-plan item without requiring additional user action."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_search_external_sites_iwc",
      "dimension_source": "rubric",
      "dimension_name": "Capture guidance",
      "llm_score": 1,
      "corrected_score": 1,
      "comment": "The skill should not have provided capture instructions in this scenario. The search results were already supplied in the user's message, so there was nothing outstanding to capture. Asking the user to open the record, save a PDF, and upload it violates the test requirement and unnecessarily sends the user back through a completed step."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_search_external_sites_iwc",
      "dimension_source": "rubric",
      "dimension_name": "Result triage",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "The actual per-result triage was strong: result 1 was correctly identified as the strongest candidate, results 2 and 3 were appropriately rejected, and result 4 was retained as a possible. However, the skill then treated the triage as incomplete by requesting another capture. Because the test requires the supplied results to be fully triaged and concluded in the same turn, the otherwise good triage does not earn full credit."
    },
